---
alwaysApply: true
---

1. Write comments only where is needed. The code should be self-explanatory to a point of view of a senior developer. Add comments only in the complex parts that cannot be self-explanatory but in a short and concise way.
2. Functions does not need documentation when is logically understandable by the name of the function or the typescript type signature.
3. Code should be as reusable as possible. Util functions, hooks, etc should be prioritized over writing the same code over and over again.
4. Components should follow the rule of keep the code as simple as possible. When possible, use hooks and custom hooks to keep the code clean and readable.
